{
  "_doc": "What Public Ledger knows about each government's itemised claims register - the abstract / warrant / voucher list of the claims its board approved for payment, itemised by payee. status = 'ingested' (the register is in Public Ledger; source = where it is posted) | 'publishes' (the government posts one; source = where; Public Ledger has not read it - 'posts', 'link_label' and 'seen' say what and where) | 'absent-verified' (someone looked at the government's own agendas, minutes and finance pages on 'checked' and found none; source = the page checked; finding = what those pages show instead; pages = everything opened) | 'unclear' (looked, could not settle; finding says why) | 'unchecked' (nobody has looked - the default). Only 'absent-verified' lets a page say the government 'does not publish' one; a publisher is never described as absent. Keys are page slugs; tools/muni_routes.py validates this file at build time. First full pass: 2026-10-05, each government's own site (WebSearch + the posted minutes/agenda PDFs); re-check before the next edition.",
